<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Antimony firm Cons Murchison sees Q4 loss.</title>
<headline>Antimony firm Cons Murchison sees Q4 loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to December 31 vs preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-capex (cts)  14 loss     vs 31 profit</p>
<p>    Shr, post-capex (cts) 111 loss    vs 54 loss</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs  -</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     0.90	  vs 2.02 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss	    0.84	  vs 2.09 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.07	  vs 0.07</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.03	  vs  -</p>
<p>    Total mining revenue  20.43	 vs 24.50</p>
<p>    Antimony revenue	8.34	  vs 9.72</p>
<p>    Gold revenue	    12.00	 vs 14.71</p>
<p>    Sundry revenue	  0.10	  vs 0.07</p>
<p>Full name: Consolidated Murchison Ltd, part of JCI Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Despite an 18 percent increase in volume sold, antimony revenue decreased by 14 percent as a result of a 19 percent drop in world price in the first two months of the quarter. Towards the end of the period prices began to recover and have since strengthened further.</p>
<p>Lower headgrades resulted in reduced gold output in the quarter of 225 kg versus 272 kg.</p>
<p>The company said that, as a result of the weakened financial postion of the company, it had decided to suspend work on the Beta shaft project while funding options were considered.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
